---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { correctionUrl, submissionUrl, REPO_URL } from '../lib/fan/contribute';
const page = new URL('/', Astro.site).href;
---
<Base title="Contribute" description="Send a correction or suggest something new for IntoTheTwilightZone.com: how fan submissions are reviewed, sourced and credited.">
  <h1>Contribute</h1>
  <p class="lead">This site is a living history, and fans know things no database does. Send a correction or tell us about something we're missing, and it goes into the same review queue as everything else on the site.</p>

  <h2>With a free account</h2>
  <div class="grid">
    <a class="card" href="/contribute/suggest/"><h3>Suggest something</h3><p>A correction, something missing (an episode detail, a person, a place, a film, a song, a book, a collectible, an homage), or an idea for the site. Follow its review on your account page.</p></a>
    <a class="card" href="/contribute/share/"><h3>Share your work</h3><p>Fan art, your photos of filming locations or memorabilia, recordings, short films, essays and memories, or a link to something worth seeing.</p></a>
    <a class="card" href="/community/"><h3>Join the forums</h3><p>Talk about episodes, the people who made them, collecting, and everything the Zone inspired.</p></a>
  </div>
  <h2>With a GitHub account</h2>
  <div class="grid">
    <a class="card" href={correctionUrl(page, 'a page')} rel="noopener"><h3>Suggest a correction on GitHub</h3><p>A wrong date, a missing credit, a better source. Every page also has its own link that fills in the address for you.</p></a>
    <a class="card" href={submissionUrl()} rel="noopener"><h3>Submit something new on GitHub</h3><p>The same kinds of additions, sent as a public issue on the site's source repository.</p></a>
  </div>

  <h2>What happens next</h2>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>You send it.</strong> With a site account, suggestions are private between you and the editor. The GitHub forms are public and need a free GitHub account.</li>
    <li><strong>It joins the review queue.</strong> Each submission becomes a row in the same queue that every record on the site passes through, marked as a fan submission.</li>
    <li><strong>It is researched and sourced.</strong> Every fact on the site needs a source, so we look for one: an official listing, an archive record, a contemporary article or the work itself.</li>
    <li><strong>The editor decides.</strong> Accepted submissions become records or corrections, credited to you if you asked to be. Declined ones get a short reason on the issue.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>What we can and can't accept</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Links, not copies.</strong> The site never re-hosts copyrighted video, audio, scans or images, and member uploads must be your own work, public domain, openly licensed, or shared with permission. Send a link to where something is legitimately available. Public-domain and openly licensed files are the exception, and we note their licence.</li>
    <li><strong>Your own words.</strong> Describe things in your own words rather than pasting text from elsewhere. Short quotations with their source are fine.</li>
    <li><strong>Connections labelled honestly.</strong> Say whether a link to the Zone is stated by the people who made something, or is a resemblance you have noticed. Both are welcome; they are labelled differently.</li>
    <li><strong>No advertising.</strong> The site is non-commercial: no shop links, affiliate codes or promotions.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="rights">Rights holders</h2>
  <p>If you represent a rights holder and have a concern about something on the site, please send a notice from the <a href="/copyright/">copyright page</a>. Content under question is taken down or corrected while the request is reviewed.</p>

  <p class="small muted">Prefer to look first? <a href={`${REPO_URL}/issues`} rel="noopener">See every open correction and submission</a>.</p>
</Base>
